From: Martin Böh <contact@martb.dev>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 02:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: support EDPD on RTL8224

The RTL8224 controls Advanced Link Down Power Saving with the same bit
as the RTL8221B, bit 2 of PHYCR1 in MMD VEND2, which is what Realtek's
own RTL8224 code writes. The driver never touches it, so it stays at
whatever the PHY came up with.

Use the EDPD tunable handlers of the RTL826x entries for it, so it can
be changed with "ethtool --set-phy-tunable <dev> energy-detect-power-down".

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Martin Böh <contact@martb.dev>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -3591,6 +3591,8 @@ static struct phy_driver realtek_drvs[]
 		.resume		= rtlgen_c45_resume,
 		.cable_test_start = rtl8224_cable_test_start,
 		.cable_test_get_status = rtl8224_cable_test_get_status,
+		.get_tunable	= rtl826x_get_tunable,
+		.set_tunable	= rtl826x_set_tunable,
 	}, {
 		PHY_ID_MATCH_EXACT(0x001cc961),
 		.name		= "RTL8366RB Gigabit Ethernet",
